# Pickthree licence

Pickthree is proprietary, closed-source software, © Solonex. It is not open source, and nothing in
this repository grants any licence to its source code.

This repository holds only the GitHub Action wrapper: metadata that runs the Pickthree container
image. You may copy, modify and redistribute the contents of *this repository* freely as part of
using Pickthree.

The software the wrapper runs is licensed, not sold. The container image is private and access to
it is granted by Solonex; nothing here grants a right to obtain, copy or redistribute it.

**You may** run the Pickthree image, in the deployments Solonex has granted you access for, to
review repositories you have access to, within the limits of your tier — free for public
repositories and for private repositories with up to 3 distinct developers per month; larger
private use requires a licence file issued by Solonex. All features are available on every tier;
licensing is by size, not by feature.

**You may not** redistribute, sublicense, sell, or offer the software as a hosted service to third
parties; reverse-engineer, modify or remove the licence verification; or circumvent the developer
count.

**No warranty.** The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. Solonex is not
liable for any damages arising from its use. Pickthree sends your code diffs to the LLM provider you
configure with your own credentials; that provider's terms apply to those requests.

Nothing in the software reports usage to Solonex: there is no telemetry and no licence server.
Licences are verified offline.

Full terms: https://pickthree.dev/terms
